<title>UK: African stock market index launched.</title>
<headline>African stock market index launched.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale and the publishing firm Africa Focus on Tuesday launched a new index designed to give an overall view of the performance of African equity markets.</p>
<p>Called the SocGen Africa Focus Africa 200 Price Index, it includes stocks of major companies in Egypt, Morocco, Zimbabwe and Kenya.</p>
<p>Stocks included were judged on market capitalisation and market liquidity.</p>
<p>&quot;We have created the index to provide investors with an instrument which measures African markets as a whole,&quot; Angelique Moorhouse of Africa Focus said in a statement.</p>
<p>Johannesburg equities are not included in the index because South Africa is a more developed market with different trading patterns, Moorhouse said.</p>
<p>The sponsors plan to include stocks from Tunisia, Nigeria, Ivory Coast, Ghana, Mauritius and Botswana at a later date. -- James Saft, London newsroom +171 542 2734</p>
